<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Borno State</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Borno State is a state in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chad">Chad</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon">Cameroon</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maiduguri">Maiduguri</a>. Created in 1976, it covers much of the heartland of the old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanem-bornu-empire">Kanem–Bornu</a> realm, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shehu-of-borno">Shehu of Borno</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">Emir</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dikwa">Dikwa</a> remain traditional rulers there. Since 2009 it has been the main centre of the Boko Haram insurgency.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/borno-state.jpg" alt="Borno State" width="320" height="172" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RAPTOR7762 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Borno_State.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
